  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <p>Looking for a calm walk near Toulon? Lac du Revest offers a green setting 20 minutes from the town centre; no dog-specific rule is published, so keep yours on a leash.</p>

      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Created in the early 20th century (dam built in 1912), this small lake, also known as Barrage du Revest or Lac de Dardennes, offers a green, peaceful setting less than 20 minutes from central Toulon — handy for a change of scenery without a long drive.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Walking around the lake with a dog is pleasant, in an atmosphere far calmer than the coastal beaches in summer. Swimming and boating are banned: the lake, fed by submerged springs, supplies drinking water to the Toulon area. Don't let your dog enter the water. The site is a Natura 2000 area. Wild camping and barbecues are also strictly banned. Parking is limited, with no real dedicated car park: you sometimes have to park fairly far away.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ideal alongside an outing on the Toulon metropolitan area's dog beaches (Le Pradet, La Seyne), for a change of scenery during the same stay.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs allowed at Lac du Revest?</h3>
      <p>No dog-specific rule is published by the town or the metropolitan authority for the walk around the lake: out of respect for the site, keep your dog on a leash and follow the signage on-site.</p>
      <h3>Can you swim with your dog?</h3>
      <p>No, swimming is banned: this lake serves as a drinking-water reserve for the Toulon metropolitan area.</p>
      <h3>Is there a car park?</h3>
      <p>Parking is limited, with no real dedicated car park — you sometimes have to park fairly far away.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Le Revest-les-Eaux, with its château, is pleasant to visit after the walk.</p>
